WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:03.033
Don't study the basics in English!

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:05.033
Why?

00:00:05.066 --> 00:00:07.066
Intentionally studying the so-called "basics" in English

00:00:07.066 --> 00:00:12.031
is a waste of time!

00:00:12.031 --> 00:00:14.031
Because learning vocabulary

00:00:14.031 --> 00:00:16.031
is a natural process.

00:00:16.031 --> 00:00:18.031
 

00:00:22.481 --> 00:00:24.481
Gradually, bit by bit,

00:00:24.481 --> 00:00:26.481
the language comes into our brains.

00:00:26.481 --> 00:00:28.481
Don't try to build a language like a house,

00:00:31.274 --> 00:00:33.274
with a foundation, a wall, and a roof.

00:00:34.795 --> 00:00:36.795
Languages are not houses!

00:00:40.702 --> 00:00:42.702
Depending on the situation, extremely basic things

00:00:42.702 --> 00:00:44.702
still take a long time for us to get accustomed to.

00:00:44.702 --> 00:00:46.702
I have studied 20 foreign languages

00:00:47.866 --> 00:00:49.866
and have experienced this process many times.

00:00:50.615 --> 00:00:52.615
For example, when I speak Japanese...

00:00:52.615 --> 00:00:54.615
I lived in Japan for 9 years.

00:00:54.615 --> 00:00:56.615
So when I speak Japanese,

00:00:56.615 --> 00:01:00.022
I don't really have any major problems.

00:01:00.022 --> 00:01:03.021
I can say what I want to say,

00:01:03.021 --> 00:01:06.021
and I can understand what others are saying.

00:01:06.021 --> 00:01:10.020
But I still make basic mistakes.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:12.020
And that is not a problem!

00:01:13.512 --> 00:01:17.485
You have a mother tongue, perhaps Japanese or French,

00:01:17.485 --> 00:01:19.485
and when you study English,

00:01:21.544 --> 00:01:23.544
grammar structures

00:01:23.544 --> 00:01:25.544
the use of words

00:01:25.544 --> 00:01:28.516
Which do we get used to first?

00:01:28.564 --> 00:01:31.549
Which comes next?

00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:34.548
There is a natural order of acquisition.

00:01:34.548 --> 00:01:37.548
Trying to deliberately memorize something 

00:01:37.548 --> 00:01:39.548
doesn't work.

00:01:39.549 --> 00:01:41.549
Instead, you should naturally

00:01:41.549 --> 00:01:43.013
listen a lot

00:01:43.013 --> 00:01:44.513
and read a lot

00:01:44.546 --> 00:01:46.546
Without feeling resistance

00:01:46.744 --> 00:01:48.744
The attitude of thinking

00:01:48.744 --> 00:01:50.744
"I want to deliberately study!"

00:01:50.744 --> 00:01:52.744
will only lead to frustration.

00:01:52.744 --> 00:01:55.744
Instead, choose fun, interesting content

00:01:55.744 --> 00:01:57.744
and listen and read a lot

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:00.010
Even if you forget again and again,

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:03.009
even if you don't understand the same part that you listen to,

00:02:03.009 --> 00:02:05.009
even if you don't understand what you read,

00:02:05.065 --> 00:02:09.042
even if you forget words you thought you had already learned

00:02:11.847 --> 00:02:13.847
even if you forget words when you read

00:02:13.848 --> 00:02:16.507
even if you forget words when you try to speak

00:02:16.981 --> 00:02:18.981
If you don't remember

00:02:18.981 --> 00:02:20.981
that's totally okay!

00:02:20.981 --> 00:02:22.981
For example, in English

00:02:22.981 --> 00:02:24.981
I go, you go, he goes

00:02:24.981 --> 00:02:27.471
You only add an "s" for "he goes"

00:02:27.472 --> 00:02:29.472
That is a very simple rule

00:02:29.472 --> 00:02:31.472
But even thought it's a simple rule,

00:02:31.472 --> 00:02:33.472
a lot of English learners make mistakes.

00:02:33.472 --> 00:02:35.472
And this is not just for Japanese people.

00:02:35.472 --> 00:02:37.472
Many other foreign learners of English

00:02:37.472 --> 00:02:39.969
struggle with the third person singular

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.208
This "He / she goes."

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:44.209
But for the purpose of communication,

00:02:44.209 --> 00:02:46.209
this is not a problem.

00:02:46.287 --> 00:02:49.561
Learning vocabulary is a matter of getting used to it.

00:02:49.562 --> 00:02:51.562
The word "study" itself [in Japanese]

00:02:51.562 --> 00:02:53.329
if you look at the characters

00:02:53.329 --> 00:02:55.072
(and I also speak Chinese)

00:02:55.072 --> 00:02:57.072
these Chinese characters originally meant

00:02:57.072 --> 00:02:59.783
"having to do things you don't want to do"

00:02:59.784 --> 00:03:01.784
Study like that,

00:03:01.784 --> 00:03:03.784
in which you intentionally struggle along,

00:03:03.784 --> 00:03:05.171
doesn't work!

00:03:05.172 --> 00:03:10.799
Instead, the fundamental way to study is to get used to the language.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.449
If you do so, you will be able to...

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:17.190
For example, in the case of English, you don't have any English habits to begin with.

00:03:17.191 --> 00:03:19.191
Because it's a foreign language,

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:22.867
it's important to learn the right habits.

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:26.179
With a great deal of time,

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:30.594
you gradually move away from the habits of your native language.

00:03:30.595 --> 00:03:32.485
And acquire the new language.

00:03:32.486 --> 00:03:34.143
In  my case, going from English to Japanese habits.

00:03:34.143 --> 00:03:35.824
In the case of Japanese people, from Japanese to English.

00:03:35.825 --> 00:03:39.798
Getting used to this new environment takes time.

00:03:39.799 --> 00:03:41.799
Acquisition takes time.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:48.000
Consciously trying to study the basics doesn't work.

00:03:48.001 --> 00:03:50.185
This is true for words

00:03:50.186 --> 00:03:52.186
and it's true for grammar.

00:03:52.187 --> 00:03:54.273
When it comes to words, it's often said that

00:03:54.273 --> 00:03:56.792
if you understand 1,000 words,

00:03:56.793 --> 00:03:58.609
no matter the sentence,

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:00.266
no matter the content,

00:04:00.266 --> 00:04:01.425
you can understand 80%.

00:04:01.425 --> 00:04:05.447
But what happens if you memorize this basic vocabulary?

00:04:05.448 --> 00:04:06.664
The result?

00:04:06.664 --> 00:04:08.345
In most conversations

00:04:08.345 --> 00:04:11.497
and for most content, sentences, and texts,

00:04:11.498 --> 00:04:15.000
these 1,000 words will not be sufficient.

00:04:15.001 --> 00:04:17.356
That last 30 percent is extremely important!

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:19.357
So be patient

00:04:19.357 --> 00:04:20.560
Take your time

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.560
And little by little

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:24.560
as you listen and read a lot

00:04:24.561 --> 00:04:25.740
the words will come in.

00:04:25.741 --> 00:04:27.373
High-frequency words

00:04:27.374 --> 00:04:29.019
because their frequency is so high

00:04:29.019 --> 00:04:30.095
because they appear so frequently

00:04:30.095 --> 00:04:33.063
they will eventually be remembered.

00:04:33.063 --> 00:04:39.205
So don't worry about trying to deliberately memorize these basic words as a goal.

00:04:39.205 --> 00:04:41.413
Don't worry so much

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:44.296
and just keep going.

00:04:44.297 --> 00:04:45.844
Oh, and one more thing...

00:04:45.845 --> 00:04:50.730
Asking someone to correct ones mistakes

00:04:50.731 --> 00:04:52.731
is useless.

00:04:52.731 --> 00:04:55.307
Even if you are corrected

00:04:55.308 --> 00:04:57.075
you will still make the same mistakes.

00:04:57.076 --> 00:05:01.968
That is, you will continue to make the same mistakes until you get used to the pattern.

00:05:01.969 --> 00:05:05.893
So just like a 2 or 3-year-old child

00:05:05.894 --> 00:05:08.911
who makes mistakes when they start speaking

00:05:08.911 --> 00:05:14.661
the brain will gradually correct the patterns naturally without formal correction.

00:05:14.662 --> 00:05:16.441
Even if 6 months pass, or a year passes,

00:05:16.442 --> 00:05:18.099
of studying English

00:05:18.099 --> 00:05:20.650
even if you always forget vocabulary

00:05:20.651 --> 00:05:23.055
or make basic mistakes

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:25.485
this is totally natural and normal!

00:05:25.485 --> 00:05:26.407
It's always this way.

00:05:26.407 --> 00:05:29.191
Even as I've studied various languages,

00:05:29.192 --> 00:05:30.616
the same thing has happened.

00:05:30.617 --> 00:05:34.014
So don't study the basics!

00:05:34.015 --> 00:05:37.289
Instead, listen and read more.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:39.682
And please speak if you have the chance.

00:05:39.683 --> 00:05:41.181
Don't feel pressure.

00:05:41.181 --> 00:05:42.630
It's a long-term battle,

00:05:42.631 --> 00:05:44.901
so just keep studying.

00:05:44.902 --> 00:05:46.498
It's okay if you forget the basics,

00:05:46.499 --> 00:05:48.769
but don't try to learn them deliberately.

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:50.770
See you later.

